00:09:48.096 --> 00:09:49.716
That wasn't entertainment.

00:09:49.776 --> 00:09:50.896
Radio isn't entertainment.

00:09:50.896 --> 00:09:51.896
That wasn't entertainment.

00:09:51.936 --> 00:09:53.396
Getting called in was the fun part, right?

00:09:54.577 --> 00:09:58.857
Basically, radio's never funny.

00:09:59.217 --> 00:10:01.678
That's a completely different argument.

00:10:01.718 --> 00:10:02.878
No, no.

00:10:02.978 --> 00:10:04.758
No, no.

00:10:04.758 --> 00:10:06.159
That part was funny.

00:10:06.299 --> 00:10:07.299
You were easy to call on.

00:10:07.479 --> 00:10:08.599
You went to all kinds of places, right?

00:10:08.999 --> 00:10:10.719
Yeah, we went to all kinds of stations.

00:10:11.279 --> 00:10:13.520
Like how the daytime slot gets called on
more easily.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:14.660
Oh, like AM and FM.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.721
He's especially good at FM stuff.

00:10:17.881 --> 00:10:18.641
Right, he's good at FM.

00:10:18.641 --> 00:10:20.881
So they keep making fun of me for that.

00:10:21.161 --> 00:10:24.242
They say stuff like, 'Your comedy is FM
comedy.'

00:10:24.242 --> 00:10:25.102
It's not FM.

00:10:25.102 --> 00:10:28.482
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:10:28.542 --> 00:10:33.063
They say FM is like, even an old lady can
send something in and get it read.

00:10:34.223 --> 00:10:35.884
You guys aren't getting any more radio
work.

00:10:35.884 --> 00:10:36.764
That's way too harsh.

00:10:36.764 --> 00:10:41.624
What I was simply frustrated about was
that everyone else had some gimmick, or a key, or something.

00:10:41.905 --> 00:10:44.925
Only we got this strong-style thing where
we just dig a hole.

00:10:45.145 --> 00:10:46.205
True.

00:10:46.565 --> 00:10:48.306
But was that even right in the first
place?

00:10:48.486 --> 00:10:54.467
That's the thing. Even now that we're
sitting here talking about it, I still don't know if that approach was actually right.

00:10:54.798 --> 00:10:56.156
We were doing The Shawshank Redemption the
whole time.

00:10:56.467 --> 00:10:57.887
Exactly.

00:10:58.247 --> 00:10:59.487
No, seriously, that's exactly what it was.

00:10:59.487 --> 00:11:00.428
Exactly.

00:11:00.428 --> 00:11:01.648
We had no idea what else to do.

00:11:02.068 --> 00:11:06.069
I still don't know whether that really
matched what the staff and the people who designed it intended.

00:11:06.189 --> 00:11:07.709
Exactly.

00:11:07.969 --> 00:11:08.649
Exactly.

00:11:08.649 --> 00:11:13.530
Even if I were in that room, I think I'd
end up deciding to dig a hole too.

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:14.750
Exactly.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.550
Because that's all there was. There was
nothing else.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:17.130
Exactly.

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.811
You'd think there'd be some button and
it'd go whirrr.

00:11:20.171 --> 00:11:21.651
You were feeling up the walls and
everything.

00:11:21.691 --> 00:11:23.491
Yeah, like there might be a hidden button
somewhere.

00:11:23.932 --> 00:11:26.592
Being barefoot pissed me off so much too.

00:11:26.812 --> 00:11:28.032
Did you have shoes in there?

00:11:28.873 --> 00:11:29.873
I did. I had them.

00:11:29.873 --> 00:11:30.873
So you did have them.

00:11:31.113 --> 00:11:32.573
You were wearing them, right?

00:11:32.613 --> 00:11:33.513
Like slippers and stuff.

00:11:33.513 --> 00:11:36.414
Yeah. We probably just never even thought
of shoes as an option.

00:11:36.414 --> 00:11:37.414
We didn't.

00:11:37.694 --> 00:11:39.614
And the whole time it was cold. My toes
were freezing too.

00:11:39.994 --> 00:11:41.434
That one was really something.

00:11:43.295 --> 00:11:47.115
The shovel was too short.

00:11:51.797 --> 00:12:01.758
No, it was tiny.

00:12:01.958 --> 00:12:03.678
Like a toy set.

00:12:03.678 --> 00:12:05.218
Like I would've asked them to prepare one
that size.

00:12:05.218 --> 00:12:08.119
Of course not. In our heads we were
picturing actual pickaxes.

00:12:08.119 --> 00:12:09.099
Like this big.

00:12:09.099 --> 00:12:10.099
Like this big.

00:12:10.199 --> 00:12:11.579
You couldn't even get any leverage.

00:12:11.639 --> 00:12:14.660
So yeah, there was a wall and all, but it
probably looked like we were just messing around.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:15.710
But at that moment...

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:17.260
...we were completely serious.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.761
And when you try to use it, it just goes
boing. Too short. No leverage.

00:12:21.021 --> 00:12:22.341
No leverage.

00:12:22.421 --> 00:12:23.421
You were really fired up in that part.

00:12:23.421 --> 00:12:24.421
I was really into it.

00:12:24.782 --> 00:12:26.942
I don't know if this came across on the
broadcast, but...

00:12:27.502 --> 00:12:30.343
there are moments when Takano's face
actually turns green.

00:12:30.343 --> 00:12:31.563
What?
What do you mean? What do you mean?

00:12:31.563 --> 00:12:32.463
I'm not joking.

00:12:32.463 --> 00:12:33.583
I'm seriously not joking.

00:12:33.583 --> 00:12:34.463
What do you mean?

00:12:34.463 --> 00:12:39.984
Like, when you're just talking to Takano
normally, there are moments when his face turns green.

00:12:39.984 --> 00:12:40.484
Green?

00:12:40.484 --> 00:12:41.224
I know exactly what you mean.

00:12:41.224 --> 00:12:42.224
You do, right?

00:12:42.425 --> 00:12:43.265
I don't.

00:12:43.265 --> 00:12:45.605
No, but really, it happens. He's normal
skin-colored right now, right?

00:12:46.105 --> 00:12:48.046
Then it turns green.

00:12:48.186 --> 00:12:50.366
So when does that happen?

00:12:50.366 --> 00:12:51.366
What kind of situation?

00:12:51.456 --> 00:12:52.456
Like when he's tired, late at night.

00:12:52.456 --> 00:12:53.456
Going pale, sure.

00:12:53.527 --> 00:12:54.227
Blue.

00:12:54.227 --> 00:12:55.107
You hear about going blue.

00:12:55.107 --> 00:12:55.767
Or ghost white.

00:12:55.767 --> 00:12:57.227
But green was a first for me.

00:12:57.227 --> 00:12:58.107
Green?

00:12:58.107 --> 00:12:59.107
And there wasn't even a mirror.

00:12:59.567 --> 00:13:01.848
So if someone says, "Dude, you're green,"
that's terrifying.

00:13:02.148 --> 00:13:05.969
Your complexion looked awful. Are you
okay, or...

00:13:07.129 --> 00:13:08.329
...did you paint yourself green or
something?

00:13:08.329 --> 00:13:09.329
I didn't.

00:13:09.529 --> 00:13:10.889
They wouldn't even give us paint.

00:13:11.269 --> 00:13:13.310
So I figured maybe you'd hidden some
somewhere.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.320
I didn't hide anything.

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:15.590
He really does turn green.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:18.391
Why would I lose my phone and everything
else and only bring paint?

00:13:19.731 --> 00:13:21.911
What kind of emergency paint would that
be?

00:13:22.752 --> 00:13:23.752
Hey, are you okay?

00:13:23.752 --> 00:13:24.752
No, I'm fine.

00:13:24.752 --> 00:13:27.252
If that's what it's like, maybe fatigue
makes him turn green.

00:13:27.252 --> 00:13:28.252
Why would that happen?

00:13:28.852 --> 00:13:32.153
It's like moss color, not human color at
all.

00:13:32.153 --> 00:13:33.073
You're saying I'm moss-colored?

00:13:33.073 --> 00:13:34.073
Seriously, seriously.

00:13:34.513 --> 00:13:35.834
That's why it's scary.

00:13:36.034 --> 00:13:37.374
It makes me sound like I'm lying.

00:13:37.374 --> 00:13:38.094
Right, right.

00:13:38.094 --> 00:13:39.534
And Takano got told that later too, right?

00:13:39.534 --> 00:13:43.535
Yeah, when he was on another show and
there was a makeup artist there...

00:13:43.535 --> 00:13:44.535
...they told him, "Your skin looks
green."

00:13:44.735 --> 00:13:45.395
What?!

00:13:45.395 --> 00:13:46.095
What do you mean?

00:13:46.095 --> 00:13:47.115
Seriously, that's why I...

00:13:47.215 --> 00:13:48.036
I'm telling you, it's true.

00:13:48.036 --> 00:13:50.556
Maybe he turns green when he's cold or
something.
Wow.

00:13:50.556 --> 00:13:53.236
Wait, is there a name for that or
something?

00:13:53.436 --> 00:13:56.097
Apparently the makeup artists said,

00:13:56.357 --> 00:13:58.057
"There are people like that."

00:13:58.077 --> 00:13:59.077
Ah, but maybe...

00:13:59.137 --> 00:14:00.558
maybe it's something to do with blood
circulation?

00:14:00.648 --> 00:14:01.938
Maybe.
Turning green.

00:14:01.938 --> 00:14:04.378
So for me it's this slightly weird phrase,
but...

00:14:04.378 --> 00:14:07.939
like, 'Get ten wanted criminals together.'

00:14:07.939 --> 00:14:08.899
Oh yeah, that was there.

00:14:08.899 --> 00:14:11.599
I was the only one saying only Miyake-san
would get that.

00:14:11.599 --> 00:14:12.599
You were saying that.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.280
I'd like that part cut, though.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.660
It had kind of a bit of this and that.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.561
Like...
I don't really know how to put it.

00:14:18.581 --> 00:14:20.401
But I totally get it.

00:14:20.401 --> 00:14:21.381
You kind of get it?

00:14:21.381 --> 00:14:22.881
Only Mitate-san makes sense to me.

00:14:23.021 --> 00:14:24.201
Like he already has that senior-guy vibe.

00:14:24.501 --> 00:14:25.602
Mitate-san is the only one that fits.

00:14:26.082 --> 00:14:28.362
Use just that part and then move on, next.

00:14:28.722 --> 00:14:29.762
Let's move on.

00:14:29.762 --> 00:14:30.382
Let's move on.

00:14:30.382 --> 00:14:32.482
Mitate's the only one I get.

00:14:32.502 --> 00:14:35.523
Mitate, Mitate, only Mitate-san fits.

00:14:35.523 --> 00:14:36.263
Are you saying he's wanted?

00:14:36.263 --> 00:14:38.783
What would you do if they made Great
Escape 2?

00:14:38.783 --> 00:14:39.784
Huh?
What if they made part 2?

00:14:39.784 --> 00:14:41.484
No way. I couldn't do it.

00:14:41.484 --> 00:14:42.484
No, this one was impossible.

00:14:42.484 --> 00:14:45.464
No, seriously, I only barely made it
through. Barely.

00:14:46.204 --> 00:14:46.985
Seriously.

00:14:46.985 --> 00:14:47.605
I was squeezing the whole time.

00:14:47.605 --> 00:14:49.785
I was. I was squeezing underwater the
whole time.

00:14:49.925 --> 00:14:52.645
Because on Wednesday they took me to that
deserted island, right?

00:14:52.825 --> 00:14:54.066
Oh yeah, that happened.

00:14:54.856 --> 00:14:55.856
Stuff like that, right?

00:14:56.166 --> 00:15:02.307
I've done all kinds of things with the
staff, and all the pranks and all those...

00:15:02.667 --> 00:15:03.787
The harsh ones.

00:15:03.987 --> 00:15:06.507
...but even compared to those, this one
was really the most...

00:15:06.547 --> 00:15:07.467
Yeah.

00:15:07.467 --> 00:15:08.288
...the hardest by far.

00:15:08.288 --> 00:15:11.988
How do we properly convey this feeling to
everyone?

00:15:12.388 --> 00:15:13.388
It just sounds like we're talking...

00:15:13.668 --> 00:15:14.668
Exactly.

00:15:14.798 --> 00:15:15.798
I wonder if it's coming across.

00:15:16.629 --> 00:15:20.709
In the end it probably isn't. It just
sounds like we're complaining, and I feel like it's going to cost us jobs.

00:15:20.829 --> 00:15:21.929
There is no upside.

00:15:22.349 --> 00:15:25.230
No, but it really is true that this was
overwhelmingly the hardest thing.

00:15:25.493 --> 00:15:26.850
So I really do want that part to come
across.

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:27.850
Yeah.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.010
Yeah.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.010
In this day and age,

00:15:31.571 --> 00:15:35.631
with DMM launching a new service, I never
thought I'd end up appearing on it.

00:15:35.931 --> 00:15:37.152
No, seriously...

00:15:37.292 --> 00:15:39.812
And that too, like, why didn't you tell us
that?

00:15:39.912 --> 00:15:40.912
What part don't you get?

00:15:40.912 --> 00:15:41.432
What part don't you get?

00:15:41.432 --> 00:15:44.653
Makio-san thinks it's How Do You Like
Wednesday, after all.

00:15:44.933 --> 00:15:46.733
Makio-san thinks it's How Do You Like
Wednesday, after all.

00:15:46.733 --> 00:15:47.733
He won't say it.

00:15:47.793 --> 00:15:48.793
He won't say it.

00:15:48.933 --> 00:15:51.974
He keeps saying he'll thank us back, but
he hasn't done anything.

00:15:51.974 --> 00:15:52.874
Like, 'I'll repay the favor.'

00:15:52.874 --> 00:15:53.434
True.

00:15:53.434 --> 00:15:53.974
He hasn't done anything.

00:15:53.974 --> 00:15:54.974
True.

00:15:55.074 --> 00:15:58.235
After making us go through something this
awful, I really want lots of people to watch it.

00:15:58.235 --> 00:15:59.075
I want them to watch.

00:15:59.075 --> 00:15:59.695
I want them to watch.

00:15:59.695 --> 00:16:01.275
Seriously.
I seriously want people to watch it.

00:16:01.275 --> 00:16:01.995
I seriously want people to watch it.

00:16:01.995 --> 00:16:04.255
Watch these three. There's more coming
too.

00:16:04.335 --> 00:16:07.256
There's still more to come, so everyone,
please look forward to it.

00:16:07.476 --> 00:16:08.476
Right.

00:16:09.597 --> 00:16:10.597
What is this?

00:16:10.818 --> 00:16:12.979
The deadliest killer of humans on Earth.

00:16:13.039 --> 00:16:15.081
This is bad, bad, bad, bad, bad, bad, bad.

00:16:17.983 --> 00:16:19.284
It's nothing but snacks.

00:16:19.685 --> 00:16:20.685
There's a door in the back.

00:16:22.466 --> 00:16:23.627
There's no entrance.

00:16:23.637 --> 00:16:24.637
Tsurugashima, huh.

00:16:24.888 --> 00:16:26.209
So the fact they used it means...

00:16:26.929 --> 00:16:29.531
Huh...? What was that?

00:16:32.415 --> 00:16:35.582
This kind of fun is impossible to escape.

00:16:35.842 --> 00:16:39.069
Now streaming exclusively on DMM TV.
DMM TV!
